  "TITLE": "The Bullwhip Effect<br>in Supply Chains",
  "LEAD": "A small wobble in what customers buy becomes a violent swing in what factories build, because every link in the chain pads its orders to cover the uncertainty it can&rsquo;t see. It&rsquo;s the same physics as a phantom traffic jam: one driver taps the brakes, each car behind brakes a little harder, and a mile back everyone is stopped for no visible reason.",
